{"extract": "Marian Lupu (Romanian: [mariˈan ˈlupu]; born 20 June 1966) is a Moldovan economist and politician who was the President of the Parliament of Moldova between 2010 and 2013. From this position he served as Acting President of Moldova from 2010 until 2012. He is currently the president of the party Respect Moldova Movement (MRM).", "links": [{"ns": 0, "title": "Court of Accounts of Moldova", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Alliance for European Integration", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Alma mater", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Andrei Cucu", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Bălți", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Communist Party of the USSR", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Democratic Party of Moldova", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Dumitru Diacov", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Eugenia Ostapciuc", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Eugeniu Nichiforciuc", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Incumbent", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Liliana Palihovici", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Maria Postoico", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Mihai Ghimpu", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Ministry of Economy (Moldova)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Moldavian SSR", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Moldova", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Moldova State University", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Moldovan Parliament", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Nicolae Timofti", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Order of the Republic (Moldova)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Parliamentary group", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Party of Communists of the Republic of Moldova", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Plekhanov Russian University of Economics", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Political party", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "President of Moldova", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "President of the Moldovan Parliament", "exists": true}, {"ns":